      "label": "Trinidad: the hurricane",
      "source": "Wikipedia, Narváez expedition",
      "cite": "narvaez-expedition",
      "text": "Two ships had just reached Trinidad when a hurricane struck. Both sank; 60 men drowned, a fifth of the horses, and the new supplies were lost."
    },
    {
      "kind": "landfall",
      "lon": -82.75,
      "lat": 27.79,
      "date": "12 Apr 1528",
      "label": "Boca Ciega Bay: the landing",
      "source": "Wikipedia, Narváez expedition",
      "cite": "narvaez-expedition",
      "text": "Land was sighted on 12 April 1528 and the expedition came ashore at the Jungle Prada site, near St. Petersburg. Where exactly in Tampa Bay they landed is argued."
    },
    {
      "kind": "event",
      "lon": -82.6,
      "lat": 27.95,
      "date": "1 May 1528",
      "label": "Tampa Bay: the force divides",
      "source": "Wikipedia, Narváez expedition",
      "cite": "narvaez-expedition",
      "text": "About 300 men marched inland while 100 men and ten women sailed on in the ships. The two parties never met again."
    },
    {
      "kind": "event",
      "lon": -84.28,
      "lat": 30.45,
      "date": "25 Jun 1528",
      "label": "Apalachee: forty houses",
      "source": "Wikipedia, Narváez expedition",
      "cite": "narvaez-expedition",
      "text": "The march entered the Apalachee village it had hoped would be rich and found about forty houses, a small outlying place and not the capital."
    },
    {
      "kind": "event",
      "lon": -84.2,
      "lat": 30.08,
      "date": "4 Aug – 22 Sep 1528",
      "label": "The Bay of Horses: five boats",
      "source": "Wikipedia, Narváez expedition",
      "cite": "narvaez-expedition",
      "text": "The men killed a horse every third day for food and for the hides and materials to build five boats, started 4 August and finished by 20 September. 242 survivors, about fifty to a boat, put to sea on 22 September."
    }
